const entries = [
  { title: 'Gravity-Well Simplest-First UX Transformation, Planetary Research Media Blueprint v1.0 (@ a9de8d8), Oct–Nov 2026 6-Model SOTA Hardware Shunt Panel (@ 6a22dee), and Nov 2026 Literature Radar Sync', date: '26 November 2026', items: [
    'Gravity-Well Simplest-First UX Architecture across research.openie.dev: introduced a global 4-altitude reading depth control (1 · Plain Story default, 2 · Visual & Hands-On, 3 · Builder & Evidence, 4 · Full Formal Paper as last resort) persisted with zero layout flash, transformed the home catalog hero with a tactile 10-second lookup-versus-inference energy micro-simulator and 3-beat And · But · Therefore narrative cards across all 29 studies, added progressive 4-rung disclosure + inline 15-second multilingual video/audio players + collapsible acronym drawers + inline glossary term tooltips on every study page (preserving 100% static HTML DOM anchors and tables), added plain-language lead cards to /about/*, and upgraded the Live Co-Pilot and /living/ hub to lead with everyday words before technical metrics.',
    'Planetary Research Media Blueprint v1.0 (@ a9de8d8) and Canonical Coverage Gate (/blueprint/, /coverage.json, /sourcesheets/, /transcripts/): expanded Research TV and Radio coverage to 29 studies, 145 films (116 horizontal HD + 29 vertical 9:16), 29/31 [G6] Whisper-large-v3-turbo (MIT) verified voiced languages and 50 captioned selector languages under clean-licence Apache-2.0 MADLAD-400 + LaBSE + multilingual-e5 [G4/G5] gates (zero CC-BY-NC MT/TTS weights), 29 Ed25519 + BLAKE3 signed [G0–G12] source sheets, 38 Mulberry + Tawasol (CC BY-SA 4.0) AAC concepts in /glossary/concepts.json (zero embedded CC BY-NC-SA pictograms), 46 zero-table Deafblind Braille HTML transcripts, 31 per-language Podcast RSS feeds + 24 kbps Opus voice notes, <1 MB mobile 15s MP4s, 17 Research Radio WAI1 episodes, and 13 interactive tutorials, backed by physical J/min production shunt telemetry in kits/planetary-media-joule/ across Jetson AGX Thor (INA238/INA3221 measured_j) and AMD Kria KV260 (INA260 SOM_5V_DC measured_j).',
    'Oct 23–Nov 24, 2026 6-Model SOTA Hardware Shunt Panel (@ 6a22dee) and LUT-Adapt Phases 35–42 (Claims LA-39..LA-67): executed confirmatory 90-instance and 300-query Zipf(0.85) crystallization benchmarks across LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B, LiquidAI/d1-2B, Qwen3.5-4B, NVIDIA Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-E4B, TML Inkling-2-Mini (26.4B-A3.4B), and PrismML Ternary-Bonsai-2.5-27B (Q2_0) on Jetson AGX Thor (INA3221/INA238 measured_j: 29.86x live stream cut to 13.27 J at 96.67% accuracy; 3.82x Q2_0->FP32 unpack tax), AMD Kria KV260 (INA260 measured_j, 0.56% drift Falsifier 6 PASS: 21.61x gross / 21.58x net cut to 25.01 J gross / 5.89 J net), and Ryzen AI Max+ 395 (RAPL reported_j: 25.84x cut), alongside LUT-Adapt Claims LA-39..LA-67 (122 six-kernel Lean 4.36.0 theorems + Inria Charon/Aeneas Rust->Lean extraction, 15/25 = 60.00% official ARC-AGI-3 supermajority via C-BFWS(R,M) + 48 KB Beneš-LUT6, license-free openXC7 XC7A200T .bit gateware, and 15.98 KB 17-export lut6_core.wasm).',
    'Late-November 2026 (arXiv 2611.*) Global Rung Radar & Pilot Foundry Sync: integrated 13 newly published Nov 2026 works across LUT-based FPGA inference (ConvLUT 2611.11507v1), audited LLM routing & abstention (RouteabilityBench 2611.34825v1, MARC 2611.20417v1, ADAPT 2611.25754v1, MeterRouter 2611.34327v1), latent handoff security & runtime attestation (Latent-in-the-Middle 2611.34278v1, Agent-as-a-Verifier 2611.34132v1, AEGIS 2611.32958v1), JEPA world-model epistemic uncertainty (2611.34830v1, ReJEPA 2611.31910v1), Lean 4 system identification (2611.18220v1), ternary prefill (BitPrefill W1.58A4 2611.26657v1), and developer cognitive load (2611.12019v1) into /radio/ and src/data/topic-foundry.json.',
  ] },
  { title: 'Post-Review Epistemic Hardening, 57-Entry Companion Chronicle, Capstone Study #29 (From Ephemeral Inference to Compiled Agency), and Sovereign Multimodal Live HMI', date: '25 November 2026', items: [
    'Post-Review Epistemic Hardening across all OpenIE surfaces: adopted Signed Provenance · Self-Checked across all internally checked artifacts and envelopes, enforced strict measurement orthogonality (measured_j ⊥ reported_j ⊥ est_j ⊥ unmetered — never summed or cross-ratioed across sensor classes), replaced metaphorical bit-equivalent phrasing with direct physical joules and finite-sample 95% Clopper-Pearson upper bounds, separated recurring content-addressed recall (C(x, z) == 1) from cold unseen generalization, and fixed Study #1–#29 evidence-class attribution on study layouts and the Contract footer.',
    'Capstone Position Study (#29 — From Ephemeral Inference to Compiled Agency, @ 813eb96 & @ cb5b641): published the six-experiment hardware synthesis package (kits/deterministic-null-suite, kits/littlebit-joule, kits/waios-mosaic-cascade) and interactive observatory at /living/compiled-agency/, documenting the 81.86x gross (71.91x net) sub-bit FP32 unpack penalty versus 4.13x packed-integer gain on AMD Kria KV260 TI INA260 (measured_j), 10/10 bit-exact waiOS 256x128 execution lanes across 6 silicon/software fabrics (BLAKE3 a541323b..., Row-77 single-weight tamper -> 4ac7c4fb... immediate halt), and the 75-cell 4-stage lookup-first cascade (26.58x KV260 & 16.26x Jetson Thor measured_j cuts).',
    'Companion Chronicle (blog.openie.dev, 57 entries + /verification/) and Sovereign Multimodal Live Voice + Video HMI (/live/): launched the full-duplex 24 kHz S2S and 100% local WebGPU FP32 Kokoro-82M (32 kHz + Perth watermark, zero browser speechSynthesis, zero fp16 fallback) voice, camera, and screen-share co-pilot across research.openie.dev, /living/, and companion surfaces.',
  ] },
  { title: 'The Communication Tool Avalanche (DES-10 & 5-host shunts), GE-H4..H9 closure, FormEBM-v3, RCE .rlib & LUT6 VCD audits, Research TV (84 films), Research Radio, and 10 Interactive Tutorials', date: '23 November 2026', items: [
    'New study (#21): The Communication Tool Avalanche, at /papers/communication-avalanche/, with 4-instrument observatory + 10-figure gallery at /living/communication-avalanche/ and full artifacts in openie-research-experiments/communication-avalanche/. Verifies 45 Lean 4.36.0 theorems (QuorumRatchet.lean, OrchestrationFlow.lean, and EnzymaticSynthesis.lean, zero sorry), executes pre-registered models CA-M1 to CA-M5, maps 38 AI milestones from 1950 to 2026 (AI01-AI38) and 18 Month/Quarter/Year/Decade milestones (HM01-HD04), and executes CTA-E1..E5 across 5 hardware/OS hosts including physical Texas Instruments INA238 (VIN L1) and INA3221 (VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS L2) current-shunt measured_j on NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor alongside 4-host reported_j: edge attestation verifies in 23.84-50.13 us (927.30 uJ Thor VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS measured_j), zero-clock wakeup eliminates 100% of empty polls across 5/5 hosts, CTA-Orchestrator reaches 59/60 (98.33%, 0 false commits) at 2.09x/14.97x higher CpJ (CTA-E2) and contains 200/200 Byzantine faults (CTA-E3), and across 100 tasks (5 regimes) where all 10 isolated AI camps C1-C10 stall at <= 49%, immediate Digital Enzymatic Synthesis (DES-10) reaches 98/100 (98.0%, 1% false commits) at 9.26x-26.87x higher Thor measured_j CpJ (75,374x lower measured_j handoff energy than NL debate). Audits 18 BCI modalities and 16 preclinical EV studies.',
    'Writing a Game Once (GE-H4..GE-H9 full 9/9 closure), FormEBM-v3, RCE Compile E4-Prelude, and LUT-Adapt Section 4.16: closed GE-H4 (-76.22% SLOC vs Unity C# across 17 .rce Forms, 0/680 trace diffs), GE-H5 (10,000-actor Q32.32 scaling at 0.058 ms C++20 -O3 vs Python 390-actor ceiling), GE-H6 (98.46% recall / F1 = 0.9922 across 260 fault modules), GE-H7 (840 Lyapunov trajectories, R^2 = 0.9940-0.9995), GE-H8 (3-OS 216,000-tick replay from 44.6 KB gzip input log D, 0/6,480 mismatches), and GE-H9 (36/36 Godot 4.7.2 headless parity); trained span-normalized two-head FormEBM-v3 in /papers/rce-jepa/ (H5 unseen beam AUROC = 0.9437, H11 94.0% strict monotonicity, resolving cross-task OOD H15 edit-size inversion from 0.2585 to 0.5278 pooled AUROC / 0.6018 large-valid vs short-invalid); added pre-compiled librce_rt.rlib as 15th tier in /papers/rce-compile/ (20.07x lower rustc -O3 compile reported_j, slashing median payback N* 28.8x from 31,080 to 1,079); and added 4-phase Verilator VCD toggle-rate + AMD DS925 switching est_j audit in /papers/lut-adapt/ Section 4.16 (361.68 est_pJ/cycle steady eval, 4.50x RAMB36E2 ENARDEN gating reduction). Synced all 19 translated papers across 8 languages (152/152 complete: true) and all 21/21 archival LaTeX PDF twins.',
    'OpenIE Research TV v3.0 (/tv/), OpenIE Research Radio (/radio/ + /radio/rss.xml), and Interactive Tutorials Hub (/tutorials/): upgraded /tv/ to v3.0 with 84 plain-language 720p MP4 research films across 4 telescoping depth slots (15s Three Plain Points, 45s Everyday Example, 90s Full Briefing, and 180s 3D Deep Cut), where every film and study card opens with the paper\'s 3 layperson bullets, passes an automated zero-acronym-soup clarity gate (lint_tv_clarity.py), and is narrated by a 21-presenter ElevenLabs eleven_v4 global studio ensemble; launched /radio/ with 8 multi-voice conversational episodes (19-persona global ensemble), synced transcripts + pop-up citation/falsifier cards, Podcast RSS 2.0 feed, and an autonomous 6-hour open-access literature scraper + deterministic <60s pilot foundry; and launched /tutorials/ with 10 guided 4-step 60fps Canvas labs (Predict -> Break -> Repair -> Verify) supporting chromeless ?embed=1 mode.',
    'Ecosystem-Wide Lean 4.36.0 & 6-Kernel bubblewrap Paranoid Hardening: audited all OpenIE formalizations against 2026 Lean 4 soundness, .olean replay, and compiler-trust disclosures (CVE-2026-72844 nested inductive .proj confusion, CVE-2026-72711 add_opaque free-variable check, #14977 Prop-structure projection tightening, #16674/#16675/#16688 forged .olean/.inductInfo replay bypasses, and #16693 native_decide / Lean.ofReduceBool), upgraded openIE-dev/rce (commit f87d6af2) from Lean 4.12.0 to Lean 4.36.0 across all 97 .lean files (5,393 theorem constants from the unchanged 1,264 source theorem/lemma declarations, 0 sorry/opaque/ofReduceBool), and verified unanimous 6/6 independent kernel acceptance under Linux bubblewrap-sandboxed lake check --paranoid (con-leche --verified, con-ron --verified, lean4lean, nanoda, leanchecker --paranoid, and Lean v4.36.0) across RCE (68,090 / 68,092 decls), Time as an Index (58,796 / 58,798 decls), The Communication Tool Avalanche (58,928 / 58,930 decls), and Downward LUT6 Compilation (58,683 / 58,685 decls, commit 1f50db59 in openie-research-experiments).',
  ] },
  { title: 'Windows 11 + DirectX 12 closure, RCE Compile energy payback & De Bruijn scale, FormEBM-v2 & 40/40 H15-Iterative, 20/20 LaTeX twins, and 144/144 sync', date: '23 November 2026', items: [
    'Writing a Game Once and Satiation Benchmark Harness: closed bare-metal Windows 11 Pro x86-64 (Intel Core i7-1165G7 + NVIDIA RTX 2060 + Intel Iris Xe) and DirectX 12 in /papers/game-engines/, /papers/satb-harness/, and openie-research-experiments/game-engines-determinism/. GE-H1 now spans 30 target x host cells across 6 machines and 3 OSs (macOS, Linux, Windows 11; including MSVC cl.exe 19.44 /O2 /fp:strict std::_Signed128) with 0/25,500 SHA-256 checkpoint mismatches; GE-H2 records the 3-OS transcendental triangle (Windows UCRT vs Linux glibc at tick 10, vs Apple libSystem at tick 37) and MSVC /fp:precise vs Clang FMA divergence at tick 192; GE-H3 spans 8 hardware GPU x API endpoints across DirectX 12, Apple Metal, and Vulkan (28/28 hardware pairs passing PSNR >= 64.16 dB and SSIM >= 0.999833; 108.34 dB same-GPU RTX 2060 DX12 vs Vulkan; 0.000% diff RTX 2060 DX12 vs RTX 4050 Vulkan). SATB adds Windows 11 as its 5th host archetype (rootless nvml.dll cumulative mJ L2 reported_j, 2.458 ms Win32 TerminateJobObject, 0 NTFS CRLF drift on 149,747 B C9, and -89.88% GetProcessTimes tick-aliasing Falsifier 3).',
    'RCE Compile: executed pre-registered E4-Energy and E5-Scale in /papers/rce-compile/, /living/rce-compile/, and openie-research-experiments/rce-compile/ (Linux Zen 5 RAPL core and APU package reported_j; measured_j unset). Across 20 exact-integer and fixed-point kernels x 14 compiler tiers (280/280 checksum-verified cells), Python to clang -O3 pays back at median N* = 2,490 runs, -O0 to -O3 at median N* = 53,464-102,720 runs, 6/20 (30%) of clang and rustc -O2 to -O3 cells never pay back (N* = infinity), and H4 Regime-B confirms runtime x power R^2 = 0.9999 vs 0.1154 static Wasm IR. Scaling E5 across 245 base programs (all 185 W1 RCE Forms + 60 C/Rust/Python kernels) and 500 execution-verified semantic mutants yields 0/500 false-positive collisions for De Bruijn nameless SHA-256 vs 150/500 (30.0%) for naive AST identifier-stripping, with 167.8x (clang -O3) and 448.5x (rustc -O3) warm-cache compilation reported_j reductions.',
    'RCE-JEPA: trained and evaluated FormEBM-v2 (5.85M trainable parameters, contrastive validity + 5-step edit-depth margin + VICReg on the strictly disjoint 1,387-Form split; 47.09 mJ RAPL core reported_j per candidate; measured_j unset) and executed H15-Iterative in /papers/rce-jepa/, /living/rce-jepa/, and openie-research-experiments/rce/bench/form-ebm-v2-and-iterative/. FormEBM-v2 meets H5 (unseen test AUROC = 0.8922 >= 0.85, 84.05% top-1 valid on solvable beams, 2.39x fewer rce check calls) and H11 (93.0% >= 80.0% strict 5-step monotonicity, mean Spearman rho = 0.9931). Under bounded deterministic checker feedback plus public stdlib/lib declaration headers (max_turns = 5, zero access to original), Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Sonnet 5.5 close 40/40 (100.0%, 0 contradictions) and xAI Grok 4.20 Reasoning closes 39/40 (97.5%, 0 contradictions); warm DNULLMM1 Gear-0 v2 replays 40/40 at 0 calls (1.771 microjoules), and the 3-Gear Zipf(0.85) stream admits 200/200 arrivals with a 16.67x frontier episode reduction.',
    'Archival LaTeX Twins, Downward LUT6 Compilation, and Multilingual Sync: published compiled archival .tex + .pdf twins for all 20/20 studies under /pdfs/latex/, merged Claims LA-11..LA-14 (openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai at af152ba) with Section 4.15 xck26 synthesis audit in /papers/lut-adapt/, and incrementally synced all updated studies across all 8 language editions (144/144 complete: true).',
  ] },
  { title: 'Multi-host hardware rails, FormJEPA-v1, cross-GPU wgpu tolerance, JCP/MEI-Tag-v1 hardware, and 144/144 full translations', date: '22 November 2026', items: [
    'Satiation Benchmark Harness and Downward LUT6 Compilation: extended /papers/satb-harness/ across four silicon archetypes with physical Texas Instruments INA238 (VIN L1) and three-channel INA3221 (VDD_GPU, VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS, VIN_SYS_5V0 L2) shunt measured_j receipts on NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor (shared host, A2 withheld per Falsifier 6), 0440 root:energy PLATYPUS-isolated RAPL + Radeon 8060S PPT on Framework AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395, and dual-level psys/package-0 RAPL reported_j on Intel Core i9-13900H; added Section 4.12 to /papers/lut-adapt/ reporting xck26-sfvc784-2LV-c full-subsystem Yosys xcup synthesis (67,366 CLB LUTs, 126 IOBs, 73 levels for clai_kv260_axi_top), read-only hw_server JTAG scan, and Vivado 2026.1 OOC scripts.',
    'RCE-JEPA and the Reality Code Engine: trained and evaluated FormJEPA-v1 (8.42M trainable parameters + EMA target encoder under VICReg on 1,387 disjoint Forms; effective rank 32.9 to 85.2; 474.8 mJ RAPL core / 6.74 J gross package reported_j at k = 16; measured_j unset) in openie-research-experiments/rce/bench/form-jepa-v1/, admitting 177/200 (88.5%) unseen synthetic Form defects, lifting the deterministic ladder to 138/151 (91.4%) at zero frontier calls, matching 35B Qwen 3.6 at 27/40 (67.5%) on the 40 residual H15 tasks, and cutting Zipf(0.85) frontier calls by 8.70x in a 3-Gear Cascade. Executed the registered 151-task rce repair rung-f criterion evaluation: rce repair criterion returns holds: false (3/119 = 2.5% > 2.0%, 3/3 mutation-gate pass, 0 contradictions), keeping rung f in observe mode.',
    'Writing a Game Once: verified 0/20,500 SHA-256 checkpoint mismatches across 25 target x host cells (5 machines, 3 ISAs: arm64, aarch64, x86_64, plus wasm32), measured cross-OS std::sin divergence at tick 10 and cross-ISA FMA divergence at tick 406, executed GE-H3 headless wgpu rendering tolerance across Apple Metal, AMD RADV Vulkan, NVIDIA RTX 4050 Vulkan, and Intel ANV Vulkan (24/24 pairs passing PSNR 64.16-72.06 dB and SSIM >= 0.999833), and launched the playable 60 Hz Q32.32 Chrono-Budget Arena with WebXR gamepad support at /living/game-engines/.',
    'Metabolic Intelligence, JouleOS, and 144/144 Multilingual Parity: published jcp-satb-cad-spine (310 tests, 78,400-pair provenance meet-semilattice, Ed25519 canonical det-CBOR JCR-1 receipts) and the MEI-JCP-Tag-v1 sovereign hardware package (0-DRC 2-layer STM32WBA52 + INA238 + FRAM PCB Gerbers/KiCad/BOM/CPL, 3D STEP/STL enclosure, and 10,000-wakeup CR2032 electro-thermal verification; board_metered is false) in openie-research-experiments/jcp-cad-mei-tag/ and /living/mei/; upgraded all 18 research papers across all 8 languages (144/144) to full complete: true editions.',
  ] },
  { title: 'Time as an Index and Satiation Benchmark Harness', date: '22 November 2026', items: [
    'New study: Time as an Index, What It Would Take to Look Up Tomorrow, at /papers/time-as-an-index/, with interactive observatory at /living/time-as-an-index/ and reproducible package in openie-research-experiments/time-as-an-index/. Audits sequential search vs lookup across closed timelike curve complexity (D-CTC = PSPACE, P-CTC = PP, unbounded Delta_2), quantum no-signalling, analog relaxation, and Hellman time-memory tradeoffs (T * M^2 = N^2); verifies 31 theorems in Lean 4.36.0 (Horizon.lean and Paradox.lean, zero sorry); executes deterministic M1 to M8 and F5 SHA-256 spectral runs (N = 65,536 digests, 0 bins below corrected p = 10^-6); and publishes 195 structured entries across TA001-TA081, AA01-AA40, and P01-P74. No hardware power monitor was attached (board_metered is false).',
    'New study: Satiation Benchmark, Reference Harness, Adapters, and Telemetry Attribution, at /papers/satb-harness/, with interactive observatory at /living/satb-harness/ and receipts in openie-research-experiments/satb-harness/. Specifies Lane B (ContextRule_v0 80% oldest-tool-output elision and Truncate_v0 8+8 KiB truncation), loopback adapter bridge Shapes D/M/H/I, a five-block system-under-test fingerprint, conformance checks C1 to C12 (12/12 passed on Apple M5 Max), and rootless telemetry levels L0 to L4 crossed with attribution labels A1 to N. Reports live C12 multi-vendor determinism probes, the 0 Hz to 100 Hz observer-effect curve (0.011 mW boundary rusage vs 66.44 mW at 10 Hz), Kepler CPU-proportional divergence (+35.86% / -32.59% on L2), 188-window Falsifier 6 baseline filtering, and 24/24 + 6/6 multi-file completion parity with Claude Code 2.1.330. Energy readings stay reported_j; measured_j is unset.',
  ] },
  { title: 'Empirical closures across RCE, RCE-VC, RCE-JEPA, Deterministic Null, Game Engines, AI Reads Human, and i18n', date: '22 November 2026', items: [
    'The Reality Code Engine and RCE-VC: synced openIE-dev/rce to commit 1762fb4b (5,537 Lean 4 theorem constants across theorems T1 to T63; 2,221/2,236 passing conformance checks with 0 failures; regenerated /rce/spec/) and openIE-dev/rce-vc to commit aba99fce (49 offline tests; 69.7 to 73.6 microseconds and 317 to 365 microjoules L3 reported_j per 100,000-unit admission), with public receipts in openie-research-experiments/rce/bench/reported-j/ (49.04 mJ per Form check; measured_j unset).',
    'RCE-JEPA: H2 is supported on Apple M5 Max reported_j (0.04904 J per Form check vs 84.25 J local Qwen 3.6 proposal, ratio 0.000582 <= 0.05). Pre-registered H15 (k = 1) and Shape D (DNULLMM1) Gear-0 results on the 40 residual tasks are filed in openie-research-experiments/rce/bench/h15-gear0/: Claude Opus 5.5 admits 34/40 (85.0%), Claude Sonnet 5.5 32/40, xAI Grok 4.20 Reasoning 31/40, OpenAI GPT-OSS-120B 29/40, local Qwen 3.6 35B-A3B 27/40, and DeepSeek V4.1 17/40; warm DNULLMM1 Gear-0 replays 34/40 at 0 model calls (1.77 microjoules lookup), hits 7/9 alpha-renamed variants via rce fmt nameless, and cuts Zipf(0.85) calls by 4.17x. No purpose-trained latent Form JEPA has been trained yet. The Laws of Coding remain the acceptance rule under test.',
    'Writing a Game Once and "AI" Reads Human: executed GE-H1 (5-target 100,000-tick Q32.32 simulation across Rust native, Rust Wasm32, C++20, Node.js BigInt, and Python 3.13 with 0/1,000 SHA-256 checkpoint mismatches and 0.103 J to 13.60 J L3 reported_j) and GE-H2 (25,000-tick float drift controls) with new observatory at /living/game-engines/; added Section 5c dual-channel Apple M5 Max reported_j across 34 parse and tiktoken workloads (280.4 nJ/record binary struct to 575,799.3 nJ/record pure-Python YAML; 109/170 L2 Falsifier 6 triggers) with upgraded observatory at /living/ai-reads-human/; added /living/latency/; and expanded multilingual coverage across all 8 languages.',
  ] },
  { title: 'Deterministic Null', date: '22 November 2026', items: [
    'New study: Deterministic Null, a Pre-Registered Control Experiment for Neural and Agentic Substrates, at /papers/deterministic-null/, with interactive living figures at /living/deterministic-null/ and public repository at openIE-dev/deterministic-null. Reports five-language bit-exact conformance (Rust, C++20, Go, Julia, Python; frozen digest 0da4df8d9ccbce1e...), Track-A (reg-exp-001, drand 6663734, 2,840 instances; 9 of 10 single-turn cells exclude neural relevance at delta = 0.05), Track-B (reg-exp-002, drand 6664089, 1,190 unique instances across Unique 3-SAT, BFCL v3, Sierra tau-bench Retail, BigCodeBench v0.1.3, and SWE-bench Verified), and exp-003 closures (OpenAI gpt-oss-120b and xAI Grok 4.20 Track-B, 49/50 extended-thinking and 50/50 O(m) clause-feedback Unique 3-SAT DRAT resolution, and 5/6 real upstream SWE-bench Verified pytest patches). Local Apple M5 Max IOReport and kernel rusage counters stay reported_j; measured_j is unset.',
  ] },
